Strong recommendation that Amazon stop using EMS!
Products are 5 stars, shipping is 1 star, average rating is 3 stars.
I don't know why Amazon would send EMS; they should recognize that it's unreliable, right? After all, computers are valuable goods!
The order for after purchase shows that it is expected to be delivered on October 20th; therefore, everyone waited at home for three days!
Why does it take four or five days to send from Xiamen to Fuzhou?
By the time I checked my shipment on Wednesday morning, it finally arrived in Fuzhou. Excited to open and receive the package, but then, without receiving any calls or messages that evening, I checked the logistics again and found out that it had been delivered earlier this afternoon, with an indication of it being personally signed for!
I was stunned momentarily!
Who am I? Where am I? Is this really my computer that I bought?
Isn't it simply suspicious of life?
He finally brought his computer back after making a round trip to the drop-off point.
The simple reason is that the delivery person got the two tracking numbers mixed up, so it's not like they lost anything.
I strongly recommend that Amazon stop using EMS; if they continue to use it in the future for their package deliveries, I will definitely not buy from them again.
